<Article
  title="Aura Farms, grown on the wall"
  description="Return to Aura. One beautiful room at a time."
  kicker="Farms"
  date="2026-09-30"
>
  <p>Aeroponics grows plants with their roots in air, misted with water and nutrients, rather than set in soil. In an Aura room the garden is a wall: vertical channels along one long side, with light for the hours the meadow cannot give.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">Why a wall, not a greenhouse beside it</RevealHeading>
  <p>The room is already closed and glazed, on a steel frame. Putting the farm in the wall keeps the harvest in the room you can lock, heat, and move. The other side can stay glass, so the meadow is still the view. It is the same object as <a href="/#shell">the room</a>, with a different long side.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">Who it is for</RevealHeading>
  <p>Buy it if you want to grow for a house, a kitchen, or a small stay. Ask Aura to build and place it if the point is food on a site you do not want to farm by hand every day. In that second case, we build the room and put it where the food is wanted. It does not yet mean a franchise counter, a brand of produce, or a guaranteed yield.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">What a yield depends on</RevealHeading>
  <p>Light, the nutrient loop, temperature, and who is there to harvest. A page cannot promise pounds per week. The enquire is where the site, the power, and the crop list get named. Greens and herbs are the honest first crop. Fruit is possible in the picture, and it is slower.</p>
  <p>A later label on this wall is in <a href="/journal/free-food-and-water">the network note</a>. The room you can ask for is on <a href="/farms">Aura Farms</a>.</p>
</Article>
